From 110f8bb4f92381a6cb7df2b1d248d1084a3b92a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 11:37:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] Compute the solar geometry block by block; physics
 checks and exports by blocks

The downscaler computes the solar geometry of each block of points and time
steps (solar_geom.window_terms once for the period, solar_geom.solar_block
per block) instead of reading ds_solar.nc, which held points x time steps
float64 arrays in memory (about 8 GB for 1000 points and 30 years). A
precomputed ds_solar is still accepted. get_solar_geom uses the same
functions (results unchanged, bit for bit); compute_solar_geometry() only
writes the file with toposcale.save_solar_geometry: true. The output store
records the solar settings in its attributes.

run_all_checks reads the outputs by blocks of time steps holding all points
(max_block_mb) and computes their solar geometry from the coordinates of
the points; the report is identical to the full-array one on Davos.

The export runner caps the memory of a block of points (max_block_mb).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
